                <pb facs="0840" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg734"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Earl of Elgin to Governor Sir W.
                    MacGregor.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Downing Street</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 24.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Referring to your telegram of the 8th September, proposals for modus vivendi,
                    including suspension of act No. 1 of this year, made to United States ambassador
                    the 3d September. Copies of correspondence went by last mail.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
